From 54378b456020c81bf72acf96ebc2848539b23859 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gili Tzabari <cowwoc2020@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 20:19:28 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] bugfix: Finish legacy Windows capture after the root process
 exits

Drain the output already buffered when capture finishes instead of waiting for inherited pipe handles held by surviving descendants. Own and close both read handles. The regression checks complete stdout and stderr beyond one read buffer, plus descendant survival.

Base: rust-v0.163.0 (83086188ae0614bd882818ff1aa23f3194962012), no prerequisite patches. Native red: run40008639744 on windows-2022 and windows-latest waits until the descendant deadline after normal root exit. Maintained just fmt-check passes. Native patched behavior remains unverified until the focused lifecycle matrix executes.
